 skills. In a rapidly changing world, it is important for students to develop the ability to think critically and creatively, as well as to collaborate and communicate effectively. This can be achieved through project-based learning, which allows students to apply their knowledge and skills to real-world problems. Furthermore, there is a need for greater integration of technology in education. Technology has the potential to enhance learning experiences, facilitate collaboration, and provide access to a wealth of information and resources. By embracing technology, educators can create more engaging and interactive learning environments that better prepare students for the digital age. In conclusion, education reform in the 21st century should focus on creating student-centered learning environments, fostering critical thinking and problem-solving skills, and integrating technology into the classroom. By doing so, we can ensure that our education systems are equipping students with the skills and knowledge they need to thrive in an ever-changing world.", "encoding_time_report": {"container_generation": 23.32, "secret_key_generation": 65.97}, "decoding_time": 0.0007588863372802734, "decoded_message": "01100011010110100101001100100010011010001111111111111101010000110101001001001011100101100110100110011000101111100100100111000101", "error_message": ""}